# ── The Gradle wrapper is TRACKED. Do not re-ignore it. ─────────────────────
#
# `gradle-wrapper.jar`, `/gradlew` and `/gradlew.bat` used to be listed here —
# they come that way from `flutter create`. The consequence (S10-3a) is that
# **the Android build was not reproducible from a clean clone**: `./gradlew`
# cannot start without its own jar, so a fresh checkout or a CI runner had
# nothing to bootstrap with. Whatever jar happened to be on the developer's
# disk was the build, and on this machine that was a Gradle 2.x-era jar
# (build receipt 2015-12-21) which cannot bootstrap the declared
# `gradle-8.12-all` at all — it fails with "Could not determine wrapper
# version. No build receipt resource found."
#
# Checking the wrapper in is what Gradle itself recommends, and it is the only
# thing that makes the declared Gradle version binding rather than advisory.
#
# ## The jar is a binary that executes on every build, so it is pinned
#
#   android/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
#   SHA-256 2db75c40782f5e8ba1fc278a5574bab070adccb2d21ca5a6e5ed840888448046
#
# Verified 2026-08-16 against Gradle's published wrapper checksums — the same
# list `gradle/wrapper-validation-action` uses. The jar changes rarely, so that
# value is shared by 8.10 through 8.13; it is the official one for the declared
# 8.12.
#
# **If you upgrade Gradle, re-verify the new jar against that list before
# committing it**, and add `gradle/actions/wrapper-validation` to CI when CI
# exists. A swapped wrapper jar runs arbitrary code on every developer's
# machine and every build agent, and it is the one file here nobody reads.
/.gradle
/captures/
/local.properties
GeneratedPluginRegistrant.java
.cxx/

# Remember to never publicly share your keystore.
# See https://flutter.dev/to/reference-keystore
key.properties
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks
